{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QExponentialExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QExponentialExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.exists_in_shuffle_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.exists_in_shuffle_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L50-L81","doc":"**Existence of the q-exponential grouplike.**\n\nOver any Hopf algebra `H` equipped with a q-Jackson derivative\n`D_q`, a coproduct `Δ`, a counit `ε`, and an element `x` such that\nthe Jackson factorials `[n]_q!` are invertible, the formal series\n`e_q = Σ x^n / [n]_q!` defines a grouplike satisfying the flow\nequation.\n\nThe construction is not a theorem of Mathlib: it requires the\nq-binomial identity\n  Δ(x^n) = Σ_k (n choose k)_q · x^k ⊗ x^(n-k)\nwhich has to be built from the q-shuffle Hopf-algebra structure.\nWe record the statement as an existence proposition; the proof\nfollows the Kassel construction in [kassel1995] §IV.2. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-exponential-exists","label":"prop:q-exponential-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.flow_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.flow_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Flow equation: D_q e_q = e_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.counit_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.counit_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Counit: ε(e_q) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.grouplike","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.grouplike","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Grouplike axiom: Δ_q(e_q) = (e_q, e_q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.D_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.D_q","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L42-L42","doc":"q-Jackson derivative on H. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.counit","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Counit on e_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.coprod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.coprod","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Coproduct on e_q: Δ_q(e_q) = e_q ⊗ e_q, encoded as `coprod : H → H × H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.e_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.e_q","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The grouplike element e_q ∈ H. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.mk","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential","kind":"structure","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L26-L48","doc":"**q-Exponential data**: an abstract grouplike of the q-shuffle\nHopf algebra, characterised by the flow equation `D_q g = g`.\n\nMirrors the canonical `def:q-exponential` definition\n(`QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/q-exponential.lean`); inlined here\nso this proposition's sibling compiles standalone (the existence\nproof needs the structure in scope). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-exponential","label":"def:q-exponential","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0}]}